msgid "IDS_PXSD110"
msgstr "Akari"

msgid "IDS_PXSD110_DESCR"
msgstr "<p>The missile destroyer Akari was built in the eastern part of the United Federation during the first decade after the emergence of the Limit. Stealthy and maneuverable, it became the perfect spy and a participant in the most dangerous sorties.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The Curator personally oversaw the selection of a commander for this ship: it had to be someone combining agility, an unconventional mind, and a slightly unhealthy recklessness, willing to take risks even when the game seemed not worth the candle.</p>"

msgid "IDS_PXSD110_FULL"
msgstr "Akari"

msgid "IDS_PXSD110_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PXSD110_YEAR"
msgstr "1959"

msgid "IDS_PXSD210"
msgstr "Nebula"

msgid "IDS_PXSD210_DESCR"
msgstr "<p>The Nebula-class destroyers were the first ships sent by the Curator's directive to investigate anomalies at the Edge. Built for swift and stealthy travel, they lacked the necessary armament to confront an intergalactic threat. Nearly all ships from the first mission were destroyed or vanished without a trace.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Six months later, one of the ships re-established contact: it had not only survived but had also managed to get remarkably close to the enemy's lair.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>It was then decided to conduct a comprehensive modification of this destroyer class, equipping them with missile armament. This made the Nebula type one of the deadliest in the universe.</p>"

msgid "IDS_PXSD210_FULL"
msgstr "Nebula"

msgid "IDS_PXSD210_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PXSD210_YEAR"
msgstr "1959"

msgid "IDS_PXSD502"
msgstr "Don de la DuQue"

msgid "IDS_PXSD502_DESCR"
msgstr "Don de la DuQue comes from a wealthy and influential duck dynasty whose history has been closely interwoven with Fishy since her very birth. The elegant Don de la DuQue is famous for his speed and maneuverability, but few know of his torpedo and mine armament or his Engine Whoosh with its increased action time. By day, he is an aristocrat with clean feathers and refined manners—a maestro of small talk. But when night falls, an avenger in a black mask and cloak takes to the streets. He takes bread from the geese and gives it to the ducks."

msgid "IDS_PXSD502_FULL"
msgstr "Don de la DuQue"

msgid "IDS_PXSD502_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PXSD502_YEAR"
msgstr "2023"

msgid "IDS_PXSD503"
msgstr "Duck Punchis"

msgid "IDS_PXSD503_DESCR"
msgstr "An officer of the law, Duck Punchis uses martial arts and special effects to teach bad guys lessons according to the Code of the Duck. He is so fast and maneuverable that geese don't even try to run from him—what's the point, when his torpedoes and mines don't leave any chances to get away? And to think they don't even know yet about his improved Engine Whoosh with its increased action time!"

msgid "IDS_PXSD503_FULL"
msgstr "Duck Punchis"

msgid "IDS_PXSD503_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PXSD503_YEAR"
msgstr "2023"

msgid "IDS_PXSD512"
msgstr "Boykiy"

msgid "IDS_PXSD512_DESCR"
msgstr "<p>The 350-ton torpedo boat project of the 'Buyny' class was ordered from the British firm Yarrow in 1897. The design was based on the series of torpedo boats of the 'Ikazuchi' type built for Japan. The ships were built in St. Petersburg in 1901–1902.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Boykiy was the lead ship in a series of ten torpedo boats, laid down in June 1901 and launched in August of the same year. It took part in the Russo-Japanese War, engaging in battles with torpedo boats and fighting in the Battle of the Yellow Sea. In December 1904, before the surrender of Port Arthur, it broke through to Chefoo, where it was interned. The ship was part of the Siberian Flotilla and underwent modernization between the wars.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>From 1914 to 1922, it was in storage in Vladivostok. During the occupation of Vladivostok by Allied forces, the ship was captured by French forces and renamed 'Quentin Roosevelt.' After the departure of the interventionist forces, the destroyer was not reactivated.</p>"

msgid "IDS_PXSD512_FULL"
msgstr "Boykiy"

msgid "IDS_PXSD512_NUMBER"
msgstr "10"

msgid "IDS_PXSD512_YEAR"
msgstr "1902"

msgid "IDS_PXSD522"
msgstr "Sazanami"

msgid "IDS_PXSD522_DESCR"
msgstr "<p>The Ikazuchi-class torpedo boats were built between 1897 and 1899 by the British firm Yarrow. The ships participated in the suppression of the Boxer Rebellion in China and then fought in the Russo-Japanese War.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Sazanami was laid down in June 1897, launched and commissioned in August 1899, and arrived in Japan in 1900. It participated in the Russo-Japanese War, engaging in battle with the Russian torpedo boat Steregushchy and capturing the severely wounded Admiral Z. Rozhestvensky, who was aboard the destroyer Bedovy during the Battle of Tsushima.</p>"

msgid "IDS_PXSD522_FULL"
msgstr "Sazanami"

msgid "IDS_PXSD522_NUMBER"
