msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M01_DESC"
msgstr "<p>The Zone emerged after the mysterious catastrophe of 2014 and forever changed the world around it. Here, the familiar laws of nature no longer apply: anomalies distort space, dangerous creatures inhabit abandoned districts, and among the ruins, one can find artifacts — rare and valuable objects with amazing properties. The Zone is dangerous, but that's precisely what makes it so alluring.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Those who dare to enter the Zone are called stalkers. They explore unknown territories, hunt for artifacts, complete tasks, and try to survive in a place where any mistake can cost a life. For some, the Zone is a way to earn money; for others, it's a source of knowledge or a place where a new life begins.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The Zone is unstable and constantly changing. Emissions turn familiar routes into traps, and danger can lurk even in the quietest places. Here, it's important not just to have weapons, but also the ability to think, adapt, and make choices.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Over time, stalkers ceased to be loners. Factions formed within the Zone — communities with their own views, goals, and methods of survival. It is they who determine the balance of power and the future of the Zone.</p>"

msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M02_DESC"
msgstr "<p>\"Rise\" was formerly a faction of fighters with a questionable hierarchy, which changed significantly with the arrival of Voroshilov.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The current \"Rise\" is a serious force, divided into two wings: the military wing, led by Chatsky, and the scientific wing, curated by Voroshilov. Both wings cooperate with each other, making joint efforts for the development of the faction.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Completely different people have found their place in \"Rise\": fighters, craftsmen, and even renowned scientists. The views of the members can also vary.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The internal structure appears to be matrix-based. Members of the corps form their own advisory bodies, which influence overall decision-making.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The faction's overall ideology is based on understanding the importance of comprehensive and independent study of the Zone, as well as protecting it from interference by state structures and large corporations that restrict access to the Zone's knowledge and resources.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The source of money for \"Rise\" is the sale of medical drugs and unique goods on the black market.</p>"

msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M03_DESC"
msgstr "<p>\"Frontier\" is a militarized stalker faction led by Davydov. One of the oldest factions in the Zone.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>\"Frontier\" is a quasi-military organization with a divisional command structure and a strict hierarchy: recruits form the rank and file, while the most experienced fighters make up the officer staff, making decisions on behalf of the faction.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>\"Frontier\" consists of various people: from former military personnel to stalkers sympathetic to the faction's ideas.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The core ideology of \"Frontier\" is the necessity of limiting any human contact with the Zone. This idea was formed under conditions of severe upheaval within the military community.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The source of money for \"Frontier\" is close cooperation with the military, as well as other official structures involved in studying and guarding the Zone.</p>"

msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M04_DESC"
msgstr "<p>\"Mercenary\" is a cartel consisting of groups of professional mercenaries and bandits, operating under the leadership of Müller.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The group is a quasi-military organization whose existence is ensured by a constant stream of contracts for various jobs within the Zone.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The \"Mercenary\" include a wide variety of people: from former professional soldiers and fighters of various armed groups to ordinary bandits looking to line their pockets. However, they all submit to the organization's leadership.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The faction's command structure is divisional: squads of fighters under the leadership of more experienced comrades form groups. The most experienced fighters—the officers—command the largest squads and form a headquarters led by Müller. The headquarters makes decisions on behalf of the group.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The \"Mercenary\" do not have a specific ideology as such, which advantageously distinguishes them from other factions. This allows them to attract people regardless of their beliefs, offering money instead of an idea.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The credit for creating a full-fledged association belongs to Müller, who forged the scattered groups of mercenaries into a monolithic structure that strives to monopolize its activities and push other players out of the market.</p>"

msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M05_DESC"
msgstr "<p>\"Covenant\" is the youngest and most unusual faction in the Zone. It is a militarized \"interest group\" led by the charismatic Metropolitan.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The ideology of the \"Covenant\" members is based on a certain mythical image—punishing and demanding atonement through suffering. The ranks of the \"Covenant\" are a motley mix: hardened criminals, impressionable loners, and ideologically charged individuals—all united by faith in the tenets of the \"Newfound Path\" and the unwavering authority of their leader.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The internal structure of the faction is divisional. Most \"Covenant\" members are rank-and-file fighters organized into small squads. Each squad is assigned a specific spiritual mentor who acts as a guide.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The faction's source of money comes from donations by rank-and-file fighters, as well as the Metropolitan's own funds, which he obtains from the secret sale of artifacts found in the Zone.</p>"

msgid "IDS_STALCRAFT_M06_DESC"
msgstr "<p>Forge-11 is the central and largest location in the Northern Zone. It is an extensive complex of buildings, industrial and urban structures, filled with anomalies, mutants, and factions in perpetual conflict, making it one of the most dangerous and yet valuable territories for exploration and resource extraction.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Recently, military forces have appeared in the north. They haven't been seen since the Perimeter Attack. Rumors spread that they discovered a passage leading to \"Area-9\", a secret shipyard with a unique experimental cruiser. Inside, there could be valuable resources, surviving equipment, and documents capable of shedding light on past events. However, the path to them is blocked: the ship is held by hostile forces, and its decks have become a deadly trap, as its anomalous generator is still operational.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>Assault is the only way to get inside. Operation participants must break through the defenses, disable the ship's systems, and drive the enemy out of \"Area-9\". Anomalous space, superior enemy forces, and the constant threat of ambushes make every step forward a trial.</p><p class=\"p_spacing\"> </p><p>The operation at Forge-11 is not just a battle, but a dangerous dive into the Zone's past, where success depends on team coordination and the readiness to go all the way.</p>"

