msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_GLOBAL_0"
msgstr "On the night of June 22, German aircraft carried out a bombing raid on the area of Polyarny — the main base of the Soviet Northern Fleet — and in the following days, naval communications and airfields were attacked. On June 29, enemy forces launched an offensive in the Murmansk direction."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_GLOBAL_1"
msgstr "The Northern Fleet played a crucial role in the liberation of the Arctic region: it supported the troops of the Karelian Front, covered allied convoys, destroyed enemy ships, and struck enemy naval bases."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP01_0"
msgstr "The German command has formed a squadron of heavy ships based in Trondheim. The likely mission of this formation is to attack Allied sea communications in the Barents Sea. Soviet submarines have been ordered to attack the enemy's large ships if they attempt to move onto convoy routes."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP01_1"
msgstr "A convoy, PQ-17, is heading toward Soviet ports. Fearing an attack by the German fleet, British naval command ordered the ships to scatter. Heavy losses are reported."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP01_2"
msgstr "The icebreaker steamship \"Alexander Sibiryakov\" reported a German warship in the Kara Sea, after which communication with the steamship was lost. Two days later, the German cruiser appeared at the entrance to Dikson and began an attack. Guard ship No. 19 laid a smoke screen and returned fire."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP01_3"
msgstr "Throughout 1942, the forces of the Northern Fleet ensured the protection of Allied Arctic convoys and supported the Karelian Front with amphibious landings."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP02_0"
msgstr "To strengthen the Northern Fleet, six submarines from the Pacific Fleet have been dispatched to Polyarny. One of them was sunk while crossing the Pacific Ocean. The submarines have already passed through the Panama Canal and are now navigating the waters of the Atlantic Ocean, near Newfoundland and Greenland."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP02_1"
msgstr "Soviet ships Baku and Razumny detected and managed to intercept a German convoy near Botsfjord. Despite poor visibility and shelling from coastal batteries, the Soviet destroyers engaged the enemy and scored several hits on the German ships."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP02_2"
msgstr "At Cape Zhelaniya on Novaya Zemlya, submarine S-101 detected a German U-boat and immediately attacked it, firing three torpedoes from its bow tubes. Through the periscope, a torpedo hit on the target was confirmed, and the enemy vessel was sunk."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP02_3"
msgstr "In 1943, the ship composition of the Northern Fleet was significantly strengthened, but at the same time, the enemy forces also increased. The situation demanded improvements in naval combat tactics."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP03_0"
msgstr "The Northern Fleet has been tasked with destroying enemy convoys. Submarines, destroyers, torpedo boats, aviation, and coastal batteries of the Northern Defense District have been deployed. These forces must deliver coordinated strikes against the convoys along their entire route."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP03_1"
msgstr "To support the troops of the Karelian Front, the command of the Northern Fleet developed Operation \"West.\" A group of ground and airborne forces from the Northern Defensive Region of the Northern Fleet was ordered to break through the enemy's defense between the mainland and the Sredny Peninsula."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP03_2"
msgstr "During the withdrawal of German troops from Northern Finland to Norway, it is possible that their combat equipment will be evacuated through the ports of the Varanger Fjord. The Northern Fleet has been tasked with destroying any enemy ships and preventing the evacuation of German troops by sea."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP03_3"
msgstr "In 1944, the Soviet Arctic was liberated: Germany's heavy industry ceased to receive valuable nickel and iron ore from the Petsamo region, and the German navy lost its bases in the Barents Sea."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP0_0"
msgstr ""
"The Northern Fleet begins landing troops on the southern shore of Bolshaya Zapadnaya Litsa Bay. The objective is to destroy enemy forces and link up with units of \n"
"the 52nd Rifle Division."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP0_1"
msgstr "The Soviet submarine M-172 infiltrated the enemy naval port at Liinakhamari. Despite the approaches to the port being covered by batteries and anti-submarine patrols, the submarine managed to break into the harbor, attacked a transport vessel located there, and escaped undetected."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP0_2"
msgstr "A Soviet-British task force, consisting of a light cruiser and four destroyers, set out to search for enemy ships along the Vardø — North Cape line. During the patrol, the Allies managed to approach the Norwegian island of Vardø and attack a German naval base."

msgid "IDS_TERRITORY_MESSAGE_TEXT_MAP0_3"
msgstr "The troops of the Karelian Front and the Northern Fleet managed to halt the advance of the German-Finnish army in the Arctic. The forces of the Soviet fleet are obstructing the maritime supply of enemy troops."

